```java
public static boolean isPointInsideTriangle(Vector3 p, Vector3 v1, Vector3 v2, Vector3 v3) {
    // Calculate vectors from p to the three vertices
    Vector3 v0 = VectorUtils.subNew(v1, p);
    Vector3 v1 = VectorUtils.subNew(v2, p);
    Vector3 v2 = VectorUtils.subNew(v3, p);

    // Calculate dot products
    double dot00 = VectorUtils.dotNew(v0, v0);
    double dot01 = VectorUtils.dotNew(v0, v1);
    double dot02 = VectorUtils.dotNew(v0, v2);
    double dot11 = VectorUtils.dotNew(v1, v1);
    double dot12 = VectorUtils.dotNew(v1, v2);

    // Compute barycentric coordinates
    double invDenom = 1 / (dot00 * dot11 - dot01 * dot01);
    double u = (dot11 * dot02 - dot01 * dot12) * invDenom;
    double v = (dot00 * dot12 - dot01 * dot02) * invDenom;

    // Check if point is in triangle
    return (u >= 0) && (v >= 0) && (u + v <= 1);
}
```

This method calculates the barycentric coordinates of the point `p` relative to the triangle formed by `v1`, `v2`, and `v3`. If all barycentric coordinates are non-negative and their sum is less than or equal to 1, the point is inside the triangle.

